{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84bd5ecaa919bc87","type":"tool_result","content":"14:**Short**: Kubernetes operator that manages the lifecycle of ModelRegistry, Catalog, and AIHub custom resources, provisioning model-registry service instances with kube-rbac-proxy authentication, PostgreSQL storage, and Gateway API or OpenShift Route ingress. [source: cmd/modelregistry.go:169, internal/controller/modelregistry_controller.go:282, internal/controller/modelcatalog_controller.go:183]\n16:**Detailed**: The model-registry-operator is a controller-runtime-based Kubernetes operator that reconciles three CRDs — ModelRegistry (v1alpha1/v1beta1), Catalog (v1alpha1), and AIHub (v1alpha1) — to provision and manage model registry service instances within the RHOAI platform. For each ModelRegistry CR, the operator creates a Deployment running the model-registry proxy backed by either PostgreSQL or MySQL storage, with an optional kube-rbac-proxy sidecar that enforces SubjectAccessReview-based authorization on the HTTPS port. The operator manages the full resource lifecycle including Services, ServiceAccounts, RBAC Roles/Bindings, Secrets, NetworkPolicies, and ingress resources (Gateway API HTTPRoutes or OpenShift Routes depending on cluster capabilities). The ModelCatalog reconciler similarly provisions a centralized catalog service with its own PostgreSQL instance. The operator detects cluster capabilities at startup — including OpenShift APIs, BYOIDC mode (where user.openshift.io is absent), Gateway API availability, and the platform Auth CRD — to conditionally create platform-specific resources. [source: internal/controller/util.go:36-39, internal/controller/config/defaults.go:197-211, internal/controller/config/templates/deployment.yaml.tmpl:220-272]\n53:| model-catalog-postgres | Controller-created Deployment | postgresql ({image}) |\n137:| model-catalog-postgres | ClusterIP | 5432/TCP | 5432 | PostgreSQL | Unknown | Unknown | Internal |\n141:| {registry-name}-postgres | ClusterIP | 5432/TCP | 5432 | PostgreSQL | Unknown | Unknown | Internal |\n246:| model-catalog-postgres | Opaque | model-catalog/catalog, model-catalog-postgres/postgresql | controller template | Unknown |\n302:- **Data storage:** Each model-registry instance connects to a PostgreSQL or MySQL database with configurable connection parameters including SSL/TLS certificates, keys, and root CA bundles mounted from Secrets and ConfigMaps. Database credentials are injected via environment variables from referenced Secrets. [source: internal/controller/config/templates/deployment.yaml.tmpl:40-68, 107-131]\n---\n---\n14:**Short**: Kubernetes operator that manages OGX inference servers on RHOAI, reconciling OGXServer custom resources into fully configured deployments with autoscaling, network policies, monitoring, and a validating admission webhook. [source: main.go:101, api/v1beta1/ogxserver_webhook.go:54, config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n16:**Detailed**: ogx-k8s-operator ships two controller-runtime binaries. The root `ogx-k8s-operator` binary runs the OGXServerReconciler, which watches OGXServer CRs (ogx.io/v1beta1) and reconciles each into a Deployment, Service, HPA, PDB, NetworkPolicy, ConfigMap, and optional Ingress and PersistentVolumeClaim. It label-filters its informer caches to only track resources with `app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: ogx-operator` and applies the cluster's OpenShift TLS profile (with an Intermediate fallback on non-OpenShift clusters) to the webhook server. The `ogx-module` binary is a separate controller-runtime operator that manages the OGX platform component CRD (components.platform.opendatahub.io/OGX) and uses odh-platform-utilities for kustomize-based manifest rendering, condition management, garbage collection, and platform detection. A `configgen` CLI generates runtime configuration from distribution specifications. A validating webhook (`vogxserver.kb.io`) enforces OGXServer schema integrity on CREATE and UPDATE operations with a Fail failure policy. [source: main.go:101-106, main.go:108-136, main.go:156-198, ogx-module/internal/controller/ogx/reconciler.go:15-20, config/webhook/manifests.yaml:2-27, Dockerfile.konflux:29]\n20:ogx-k8s-operator follows a dual-binary operator pattern common in the RHOAI platform. The root operator (`ogx-k8s-operator`) owns the user-facing OGXServer CR lifecycle, while `ogx-module` manages the platform-level OGX component CRD that the RHOAI operator uses to install and configure OGX itself. This separation keeps the user-facing reconciliation loop independent of the platform bootstrapping logic.\n22:The OGXServerReconciler owns a broad set of child resources—Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, HPAs, PDBs, NetworkPolicies, Ingresses, PVCs, and Secrets—and uses label-scoped informer caches (`app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: ogx-operator`) to reduce watch pressure on the API server. It also watches Secrets and ConfigMaps with a dedicated label selector rather than listing the entire namespace, which is a meaningful isolation boundary in multi-tenant clusters. A legacy adoption path exists for migrating pre-existing resources under operator management (controllers/legacy_adoption.go).\n49:| OGXServer controller | Controller | Reconciles OGXServer resources |\n67:| ogx.io | v1beta1 | OGXServer | Namespaced | Core API | Custom resource managed by ogx-k8s-operator |\n80:| /validate-ogx-io-v1beta1-ogxserver | POST |  | HTTPS | Unknown | TLS | Kubernetes admission |  | Validating admission webhook |\n163:| ogx-k8s-operator-manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n164:| ogx-k8s-operator-manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/finalizers | update |\n165:| ogx-k8s-operator-manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get, patch, update |\n173:| ogx-k8s-operator-ogxserver-viewer-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | get, list, watch |\n174:| ogx-k8s-operator-ogxserver-viewer-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get |\n175:| ogx-k8s-operator-ogxserver-editor-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n176:| ogx-k8s-operator-ogxserver-editor-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get |\n179:| ogxserver-editor-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n180:| ogxserver-editor-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get |\n181:| ogxserver-viewer-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | get, list, watch |\n182:| ogxserver-viewer-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get |\n194:| manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n195:| manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/finalizers | update |\n196:| manager-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get, patch, update |\n217:| manager-cluster-role | ogx.io | ogxservers | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n218:| manager-cluster-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/status | get, patch, update |\n219:| manager-cluster-role | ogx.io | ogxservers/finalizers | update |\n293:| vogxserver.kb.io | Validating | /validate-ogx-io-v1beta1-ogxserver |  | Fail | ogxservers | CREATE, UPDATE |  |\n297:- **OGXServer reconciliation:** A user creates an OGXServer CR in a namespace. The OGXServerReconciler watches for these CRs and reconciles each into a Deployment running the inference server image, along with a Service, optional HPA, PDB, NetworkPolicy, ConfigMap, Ingress, and PVC. The reconciler reads Secrets (labeled with the watch label) for model credentials and ConfigMaps for runtime configuration. All child resources are owned by the OGXServer CR, enabling garbage collection on deletion. [source: main.go:101-106, main.go:108-136, config/rbac/role.yaml:6-30]\n299:- **Admission control:** The ValidatingWebhookConfiguration routes CREATE and UPDATE operations on ogxservers to the `/validate-ogx-io-v1beta1-ogxserver` endpoint served by the ogx-k8s-operator webhook server on port 9443 with TLS. The webhook enforces schema validation with a Fail failure policy. [source: config/webhook/manifests.yaml:2-27, config/webhook/service.yaml:1, api/v1beta1/ogxserver_webhook.go:54]\n305:- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n307:- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Watches); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]\n308:- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create, delete, get, list, patch, update operations by OGXServerReconciler. [source: cmd/configgen/main.go:59, 221, config/rbac/auth_proxy_service.yaml:1, config/rbac/role.yaml:2, config/webhook/service.yaml:1]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a69fe9ec9252deb2","agent_id":"a890b7bc884117537","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"6ecf6ed6-cfcb-4749-a9fb-5f9cb7d910ff","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:18:56.509Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84bd5ecaa919bc87","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
