{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b6e7bafa-59c2-4cb4-9549-acd4ba977b90","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-868855b89a022b7a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-msic8a2n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E001.md","content":"# Decide the provisioning approach for the Gen AI Studio default pgvector vector store\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the one genuine unknown that gates all provisioning implementation for\nthe default vector store strategy: which of three bounded paths Gen AI Studio uses to make a\nPostgreSQL/pgvector instance available to playground RAG workflows in the target RHOAI release —\noperator-based provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard\noperator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164), BFF-managed self-provisioning by the gen-ai\nbackend-for-frontend, or a bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration path for users. It also confirms\nthe scoping model for the default store (per-namespace vs per-instance isolation). The Staff\nEngineer Input directs the development team to define a go/no-go gate for this decision as part of\nsprint planning; this investigation produces that decision.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Track the delivery status of RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization) against the\n  RHOAI 3.5 timeline. It is a hard dependency for the operator-based path: until it delivers, there\n  is no RHOAI-controlled operator where PostgreSQL lifecycle management can live. The upstream\n  ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n- Define the go/no-go criteria for the release decision: the latest date at which each path remains\n  viable for the release, and the evidence each path needs (operator layer availability, BFF\n  provisioning design feasibility, acceptance of a degraded bring-your-own experience).\n- Evaluate the three provisioning paths against: lifecycle management (cleanup on playground\n  deletion, pod-restart handling, credential rotation — the BFF is not an operator with a\n  reconciliation loop), multi-tenant isolation, and portability to the platform-provided shared\n  PostgreSQL managed via the DSC that is planned for RHOAI 3.6 (for 3.5, Gen AI Studio must\n  provision its own PostgreSQL instance).\n- Confirm the scoping model for the default vector store. Per-namespace isolation is the preferred\n  model; the per-instance motivation came from Auto Rag, which is out of scope for this strategy\n  (Auto Rag compatibility is addressed in RHAISTRAT-7824 for RHOAI 3.6).\n- Produce a decision record that names the selected provisioning path, the go/no-go criteria, the\n  evidence used, and the confirmed scoping model, and hand it to sprint planning for scheduling of\n  the corresponding implementation work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written decision record exists that names the selected provisioning path (operator-based,\n  BFF-managed, or bring-your-own PostgreSQL) together with the go/no-go criteria and the evidence\n  used to select it.\n- The record states the assessed delivery status of RHAISTRAT-7164 and the date or trigger after\n  which each fallback path applies for the release.\n- The scoping model (per-namespace or per-instance isolation) for the default vector store is\n  confirmed and recorded in the decision record.\n- The decision, including its implications for the out-of-the-box experience if the\n  bring-your-own fallback is selected, is presented at sprint planning and the outcome is recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, e.g. per-namespace isolation)** — the scoping model is decided here\n  and inherited by the provisioning implementations.\n- **AC-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store)** — this decision determines which provisioning\n  implementation can satisfy the no-manual-setup requirement for the release.\n- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — the decision record confirms every\n  candidate path provisions an external PostgreSQL process rather than an inline provider.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73907,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a69fe9ec9252deb2","agent_id":"a890b7bc884117537","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"d3e6da5d-dc53-47f2-bf37-4346c247d1ff","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:24:48.250Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
