{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-63aa7fe8-234d-42d2-9458-ff0f219f26b4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cfe81ced61f5e01","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-msic8a2n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n\n## Description\n\nSelected only if the provisioning-approach decision confirms the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\ndelivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) will be available for the\ntarget release: implements PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator layer,\nfollowing the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL auto-provisioning pattern, so that Gen AI Studio\nplaygrounds with RAG get an auto-provisioned pgvector-backed PostgreSQL instance with no manual\nuser setup. The ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning\nlogic, which is why the work belongs in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement reconciliation of a per-namespace pgvector PostgreSQL instance for Gen AI Studio\n  playgrounds in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer: Deployment, Service, Secret, and persistent\n  storage, created and owned via the operator's reconciliation loop.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`)\n  — no custom image build and no Konflux onboarding; the model-registry operator already uses this\n  image as its auto-provisioned database image.\n- Follow the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL provisioning pattern for resource\n  requests/limits, credential handling, and child-resource ownership (garbage collection on\n  deletion).\n- Scope instances per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the preferred multi-tenant model;\n  confirm against the decision record's scoping outcome).\n- Expose the provisioned connection details (secret/connection string) so the gen-ai\n  backend-for-frontend can consume them when creating playground OGX instances.\n- Verify disconnected-install coverage for the PostgreSQL image (the rhods-operator CSV\n  RELATED_IMAGE entry claimed by the strategy could not be corroborated against the architecture\n  context and must be confirmed during implementation).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled in a namespace results in an auto-provisioned\n  PostgreSQL instance with pgvector available, with no manual user setup steps.\n- Instances are isolated per namespace (multi-tenant scoping per the decision record).\n- Resource requests/limits start from the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL sizing, adjusted per\n  the pgvector benchmark findings if needed.\n- The operator reconciliation loop manages the full instance lifecycle: creation with the\n  playground, deletion cleanup, and recovery from drift.\n- Provisioning uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector; no custom image is built.\n- The provisioned connection details are available as a consumable secret/connection reference for\n  the playground OGX instance configuration.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — delivered by\n  this epic together with the BFF wiring that consumes it.\n- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance\n  is an external process managed by the operator, not an inline provider.\n- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation)** — per-namespace instance scoping.\n- **AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments)** — sizing derived from the\n  model-registry operator's PostgreSQL references and the benchmark findings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75917,"output_tokens":0},"c