{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e5883125-5331-4661-842c-dbc7a49d5b93","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a319eaed606122b2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-msic8a2n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances to the operator-provisioned pgvector vector store\n\n## Description\n\nSelected only if the operator-based provisioning path is chosen: extends the Gen AI Studio gen-ai\nbackend-for-frontend (in the odh-dashboard repository) so that playground OGXServer instances\ncreated for RAG-enabled playgrounds are configured with the remote pgvector vector_io provider\npointing at the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL instance. The OGX application storage backend stays\non its existing SQLite default — only the vector_io provider configuration changes. The existing\nremote vector store implementation in OGX is largely reusable; the integration work is\nconfiguration wiring, not provider development.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation (where OGX storage is currently configured,\n  in the Go BFF code that builds the OGXServer spec for the playground) to enable the remote\n  pgvector vector_io provider (`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) and consume the operator-provisioned connection\n  details for it.\n- Keep OGX application storage on its existing SQLite default; do not consolidate vector and\n  application storage in a single database and do not introduce any SQLite-to-PostgreSQL\n  application-storage migration path.\n- Provide a configuration-level rollback path: because this wiring replaces the vector storage\n  previously served by the inline provider being removed from the OGX distribution\n  (RHAISTRAT-7474), the pgvector vector_io configuration must be revertible to the prior\n  configuration without code changes if a regression is found.\n- Document that the default store is positioned for development experimentation: users with\n  production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database (no migration-path\n  feature is built in this epic).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Creating a RAG-enabled playground results in an OGX instance whose vector_io provider is remote\n  pgvector backed by the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL instance, with no manual user\n  configuration.\n- Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows (document upload, ingestion, retrieval-augmented chat)\n  function against the wired instance with no loss of current capability.\n- OGX application storage remains on the SQLite default; only the vector_io provider configuration\n  changes.\n- The pgvector vector_io configuration can be reverted to the prior configuration without code\n  changes (configuration-level rollback), preserving a safety margin before inline providers are\n  removed from the OGX distribution.\n- All changes pass the odh-dashboard repository's existing build and CI pipeline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — completes the\n  out-of-the-box path by consuming the operator-provisioned instance automatically.\n- **AC-2 (Playground RAG workflows function, no loss of capability)** — the wiring epic carries the\n  end-to-end workflow AC on the same configuration surface it edits.\n- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — retrieval goes to the external\n  PostgreSQL process via the remote provider.\n- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping)** — connection is scoped to the namespace-isolated instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76828,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a69fe9ec9252deb2","agent_id":"a890b7bc884117537","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"9b8f0e16-ac37-4a1e-a8d3