t that the deciding fact is external delivery timing\n88\tand a sprint-planning governance decision). Implementation epics use `ai_signals` and\n89\tInvestigation uses `investigation_signals` — no type mismatch. architecture_claims: 1 rationales\n90\tcheck out against `.context`: pgvector/PGVector is listed in `ogx-distribution.md`, the\n91\tmodel-registry-operator PostgreSQL auto-provisioning pattern is in `model-registry-operator.md`,\n92\tthe gen-ai BFF is in `odh-dashboard.md`, and the un-corroborated rhods-operator CSV\n93\tRELATED_IMAGE claim is correctly flagged as a health warning rather than asserted (rhods-operator\n94\tarchitecture context indeed contains no PostgreSQL/RELATED_IMAGE references). One calibration\n95\tinconsistency: `human_process_gates` is scored 0 for BRANCH-A-E003 (\"no approval gates beyond\n96\tnormal code review\") and BRANCH-C-E003 (\"normal docs review\") but 1 for BRANCH-A-E004 and\n97\tBRANCH-B-E003 (\"none beyond normal code review\") — the same condition receives different values\n98\tacross sibling epics. Arguable values, not rubric contradictions.\n99\t\n100\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n101\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy and staff input. Rule-mandated ACs are\n102\tpresent: configuration-level rollback ACs on both replacement-surface epics (BRANCH-A-E004,\n103\tBRANCH-B-E003) and revert documentation in BRANCH-C-E003; technical review of documentation in\n104\tBRANCH-C-E003; build/CI pipeline ACs on the odh-dashboard epics. No externally-controlled\n105\tpreconditions misfiled as ACs. No draft-ID references in epic bodies (only full RHAISTRAT-8004-*\n106\tIDs). One minor gap: BRANCH-A-E003's scope includes verifying disconnected-install coverage of\n107\tthe PostgreSQL image (the un-corroborated CSV claim), but no acceptance criterion covers that\n108\tverification — add an AC or move it to Risks/Notes so the outcome is checkable.\n109\t\n110\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n111\tAll in-scope s