{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b632b9cb8c23d57f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances to the operator-provisioned pgvector\n4\t  vector store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the operator-based path is not selected, this wiring is not\n18\t    built; the equivalent vector_io wiring is carried by whichever branch the go/no-go\n19\t    decision selects (BFF-managed provisioning or the bring-your-own configuration\n20\t    path).\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: 1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 8\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances to the operator-provisioned pgvector vector store\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tSelected only if the operator-based provisioning path is chosen: extends the Gen AI Studio gen-ai\n42\tbackend-for-frontend (in the odh-dashboard repository) so that playground OGXServer instances\n43\tcreated for RAG-enabled playgrounds are configured with the remote pgvector vector_io provider\n44\tpointing at the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL instance. The OGX application storage backend stays\n45\ton its existing SQLite default — only the vector_io provider configuration changes. The existing\n46\tremote vector store implementation in OGX is largely reusable; the integration work is\n47\tconfiguration wiring, not provider development.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation (where OGX storage is currently configured,\n52\t  in the Go BFF code that builds the OGXServer spec for the playground) to enable the remote\n53\t  pgvector vector_io provider (`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) and consume the operator-provisioned connection\n54\t  details for it.\n55\t- Keep OGX application storage on its existing SQLite default; do not consolidate vector and\n56\t  application storage in a single database and do not introduce any SQLite-to-PostgreSQL\n57\t  application-storage migration path.\n58\t- Provide a configuration-level rollback path: because this wiring replaces the vector storage\n59\t  previously served by the inline provider being removed from the OGX distribution\n60\t  (RHAISTRAT-7474), the pgvector vector_io configuration must be revertible to the prior\n61\t  configuration without code changes if a regression is found.\n62\t- Document that the default store is positioned for development experimentation: users with\n63\t  production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database (no migration-path\n64\t  feature is built in this epic).\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Creating a RAG-enabled playground results in an OGX instance whose vector_io provider is remote\n69\t  pgvector backed by the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL instance, with no manual user\n70\t  configuration.\n71\t- Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows (document upload, ingestion, retrieval-augmented chat)\n72\t  function against the wired instance with no loss of current capability.\n73\t- OGX application storage remains on the SQLite default; only the vector_io provider configuration\n74\t  changes.\n75\t- The pgvector vector_io configuration can be reverted to the prior configuration without code\n76\t  changes (configuration-level rollback), preserving a safety margin before inline providers are\n77\t  removed from the OGX distribution.\n78\t- All changes pass the odh-dashboard repository's existing build and CI pipeline.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — completes the\n83\t  out-of-the-box path by consuming the operator-provisioned instance automatically.\n84\t- **AC-2 (Playground RAG workflows function, no loss of capability)** — the wiring epic carries the\n85\t  end-to-end workflow AC on the same configuration surface it edits.\n86\t- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — retrieval goes to the external\n87\t  PostgreSQL process via the remote provider.\n88\t- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping)** — connection is scoped to the namespace-isolated instance.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b646f377ae1a5e","agent_id":"add4827a4759769c5","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"be363171-6ac0-4203-8369-0a171298121b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:31:28.654Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b632b9cb8c23d57f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
