{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8a98e802ce31fbe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E003\n3\ttitle: Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration path for Gen AI Studio RAG\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If either self-provisioning path (operator-based or BFF-managed)\n16\t    is viable for the release, the bring-your-own fallback is not built and the out-of-the-box\n17\t    experience is preserved.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 7\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration path for Gen AI Studio RAG\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tSelected only if the provisioning-approach decision rules out both self-provisioning paths for the\n39\trelease: the degraded fallback in which customers bring their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities\n40\tin the Playground. Users manually configure the OGXServer custom resource spec with their\n41\tPostgreSQL/pgvector connection details. This path does not satisfy the out-of-the-box experience\n42\tthe strategy asks for — it is a release fallback that aligns with the breaking changes introduced\n43\tin OGX 1.0, and its limitations must be explicit.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Validate the OGXServer custom resource configuration path for a user-supplied\n48\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector connection: connection details supplied via secret, consumed by the OGX\n49\t  instance's remote pgvector vector_io provider (`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`).\n50\t- Verify that OGX application storage is unaffected (remains on its SQLite default) when only the\n51\t  vector_io provider is pointed at the user-supplied database — no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL\n52\t  application-storage migration is involved.\n53\t- Document the supported setup steps: creating the connection secret, the OGXServer spec fields\n54\t  involved, enabling the pgvector vector_io provider, and the scope limitations (development\n55\t  experimentation; production-scale vector workloads belong on an external vector database).\n56\t- Document explicitly that this path requires manual provisioning and therefore does not meet the\n57\t  strategy's out-of-the-box acceptance criterion; the gap is a known consequence of the fallback\n58\t  decision.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- A validated configuration path exists for using an external, user-provided PostgreSQL/pgvector\n63\t  instance with a playground OGX instance (OGXServer spec with user-supplied connection details\n64\t  via secret).\n65\t- Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows function against the user-provided store via the remote\n66\t  pgvector vector_io provider with no loss of current capability for users who complete the setup.\n67\t- Setup documentation exists covering secret creation, the OGXServer spec fields, enabling the\n68\t  pgvector vector_io provider, and reverting the configuration; the documentation is technically\n69\t  reviewed against the validated configuration.\n70\t- OGX application storage remains on the SQLite default; only the vector_io provider configuration\n71\t  changes.\n72\t- The manual-setup limitation versus the out-of-the-box experience is documented and communicated\n73\t  as a release note item.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- **AC-2 (Playground RAG workflows function, no loss of capability)** — satisfied for users who\n78\t  provision and configure their own store.\n79\t- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — the store is an external\n80\t  user-provided PostgreSQL process.\n81\t- **AC-1 (out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — **not satisfied by this branch**; this is the\n82\t  documented degraded fallback (see the decomposition summary's health warnings). Recorded here so\n83\t  reviewers see the gap is analyzed rather than missed.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b646f377ae1a5e","agent_id":"add4827a4759769c5","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"99d71948-a65a-4b1f-8867-15dbe4ab7b0e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:31:29.887Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8a98e802ce31fbe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
