{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5ad37c16e15efe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Benchmark pgvector and validate Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Benchmark pgvector and validate Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the sprint-1 risk-reduction validation for choosing pgvector as the default\n34\tvector store for Gen AI Studio: a benchmark comparing pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline,\n35\tand an end-to-end validation of Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows against an OGX instance\n36\tconfigured with the remote pgvector vector_io provider. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the default\n37\tpgvector instance is meant for development experimentation — strict latency SLAs are not required;\n38\tthe benchmark verifies pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline,\n39\tnot that it meets a specific threshold. This validation is scoped to Gen AI Studio Playground RAG\n40\tworkflows only; Auto Rag compatibility is out of scope (RHAISTRAT-7824).\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Stand up a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image\n45\t  (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` includes pgvector out of the box; no custom image build\n46\t  and no Konflux onboarding are needed). A manually provisioned test instance is sufficient — this\n47\t  epic does not depend on any product provisioning path.\n48\t- Configure an OGX server instance with the remote pgvector vector_io provider (enabled via the\n49\t  `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` provider configuration), leaving OGX application storage on its existing SQLite\n50\t  default. Vector storage and application storage are independent configurations; there is no\n51\t  SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration concern because application storage is not being touched.\n52\t- Exercise Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows end to end (document upload, ingestion,\n53\t  retrieval-augmented chat) over representative small document sets.\n54\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline metrics for the same operations and measure pgvector against\n55\t  it. Typical Playground RAG usage involves small document sets, so flat scan (no vector index) is\n56\t  the expected operating mode.\n57\t- Record recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits, starting from the model-registry\n58\t  operator's PostgreSQL sizing as the reference point.\n59\t- Validate that the OGX distribution functions unchanged with the remote pgvector provider enabled:\n60\t  the existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable, and no OGX distribution code\n61\t  changes are expected (passive validation of the distribution).\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A benchmark report exists that captures inline Milvus baseline metrics and pgvector metrics for\n66\t  the same representative Playground RAG operations (ingestion and retrieval over small document\n67\t  sets).\n68\t- Measured pgvector performance is within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline\n69\t  for those operations.\n70\t- Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows (document upload, ingestion, retrieval-augmented chat)\n71\t  complete successfully against the pgvector-backed OGX instance with no loss of current capability.\n72\t- Flat scan (no vector index) is confirmed sufficient for typical Playground document-set sizes, or\n73\t  the specific size threshold at which an index becomes necessary is documented.\n74\t- Recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are recorded, with the model-registry operator's\n75\t  PostgreSQL sizing as the stated starting point.\n76\t- OGX application storage remains on its SQLite default throughout the validation; no\n77\t  application-storage migration is performed or required.\n78\t- The OGX distribution requires no code changes to serve the remote pgvector vector_io provider, or\n79\t  any changes found are documented and fed back into the strategy.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- **AC-2 (Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of\n84\t  current capability)** — validated end to end here.\n85\t- **AC-4 (default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** —\n86\t  validated: retrieval goes through the remote pgvector provider against an external PostgreSQL\n87\t  process, not an inline provider.\n88\t- **AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments)** — the benchmark and the\n89\t  recorded sizing recommendation are the evidence.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9636ee73fa8fca7","agent_id":"a3983a4f5ffc7ae27","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"fb97d43e-c88d-4c8e-bc24-cf9427373fd8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:33:44.218Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d5ad37c16e15efe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
