{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-916ec3703d2fb91a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: AI Core Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer (RHAISTRAT-7164) is not\n16\t    available for the release, operator-based provisioning is not built; the go/no-go\n17\t    decision selects the BFF-managed or bring-your-own path instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tSelected only if the provisioning-approach decision confirms the RHOAI-controlled operator layer\n39\tdelivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) will be available for the\n40\ttarget release: implements PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator layer,\n41\tfollowing the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL auto-provisioning pattern, so that Gen AI Studio\n42\tplaygrounds with RAG get an auto-provisioned pgvector-backed PostgreSQL instance with no manual\n43\tuser setup. The ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning\n44\tlogic, which is why the work belongs in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement reconciliation of a per-namespace pgvector PostgreSQL instance for Gen AI Studio\n49\t  playgrounds in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer: Deployment, Service, Secret, and persistent\n50\t  storage, created and owned via the operator's reconciliation loop.\n51\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`)\n52\t  — no custom image build and no Konflux onboarding; the model-registry operator already uses this\n53\t  image as its auto-provisioned database image.\n54\t- Follow the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL provisioning pattern for resource\n55\t  requests/limits, credential handling, and child-resource ownership (garbage collection on\n56\t  deletion).\n57\t- Scope instances per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the preferred multi-tenant model;\n58\t  confirm against the decision record's scoping outcome).\n59\t- Expose the provisioned connection details (secret/connection string) so the gen-ai\n60\t  backend-for-frontend can consume them when creating playground OGX instances.\n61\t- Verify disconnected-install coverage for the PostgreSQL image (the rhods-operator CSV\n62\t  RELATED_IMAGE entry claimed by the strategy could not be corroborated against the architecture\n63\t  context and must be confirmed during implementation).\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled in a namespace results in an auto-provisioned\n68\t  PostgreSQL instance with pgvector available, with no manual user setup steps.\n69\t- Instances are isolated per namespace (multi-tenant scoping per the decision record).\n70\t- Resource requests/limits start from the model-registry operator's PostgreSQL sizing, adjusted per\n71\t  the pgvector benchmark findings if needed.\n72\t- The operator reconciliation loop manages the full instance lifecycle: creation with the\n73\t  playground, deletion cleanup, and recovery from drift.\n74\t- Provisioning uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector; no custom image is built.\n75\t- The provisioned connection details are available as a consumable secret/connection reference for\n76\t  the playground OGX instance configuration.\n77\t- Disconnected-install coverage for the PostgreSQL image is verified and the outcome recorded:\n78\t  either the rhods-operator CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` entry (or equivalent\n79\t  disconnected-install mirroring configuration) is confirmed to cover\n80\t  `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`, or the gap is documented and raised against the\n81\t  strategy before release.\n82\t\n83\t## HLR Traceability\n84\t\n85\t- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — delivered by\n86\t  this epic together with the BFF wiring that consumes it.\n87\t- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance\n88\t  is an external process managed by the operator, not an inline provider.\n89\t- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation)** — per-namespace instance scoping.\n90\t- **AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments)** — sizing derived from the\n91\t  model-registry operator's PostgreSQL references and the benchmark findings.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9636ee73fa8fca7","agent_id":"a3983a4f5ffc7ae27","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"acadff6b-6e9d-4773-9f60-c79ad4b899cd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:33:47.340Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-916ec3703d2fb91a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
