{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a21ec3a40dc247f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E003\n3\ttitle: BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the go/no-go decision selects the operator-based path or accepts\n16\t    the bring-your-own fallback, BFF-managed provisioning is not built; the operator\n17\t    path delivers provisioning instead, or users supply their own PostgreSQL per the\n18\t    documented configuration path.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 8\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tSelected only if the provisioning-approach decision rules out the operator-based path for the\n40\trelease (the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator modularization,\n41\tRHAISTRAT-7164, not landing in time): the Gen AI Studio gen-ai backend-for-frontend provisions the\n42\tPostgreSQL/pgvector instance directly — similar to how the BFF currently provisions guardrails\n43\tinfrastructure — creating the PostgreSQL Deployment, Service, PVC, and Secret when a playground\n44\twith RAG is configured and no suitable instance exists in the namespace, and wiring the playground\n45\tOGX instance's vector_io provider to it.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Implement BFF-managed provisioning: when a playground with RAG is configured and no suitable\n50\t  PostgreSQL instance exists in the namespace, the gen-ai BFF creates the PostgreSQL Deployment,\n51\t  Service, PVC, and Secret using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector\n52\t  (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`; no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding).\n53\t- Configure the playground OGXServer instance's remote pgvector vector_io provider\n54\t  (`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) to consume the provisioned instance; keep OGX application storage on its\n55\t  SQLite default (vector storage and application storage are independent configurations — no\n56\t  migration path is built).\n57\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC becomes\n58\t  available (RHOAI 3.6), the BFF must be able to consume the shared connection string rather than\n59\t  self-provisioning, without a rewrite of this feature.\n60\t- Address lifecycle management explicitly — the BFF is not an operator with a reconciliation loop:\n61\t  cleanup on playground deletion, handling of pod restarts (no orphaned or duplicate instances),\n62\t  and credential rotation need explicit design and tests.\n63\t- Scope instances per namespace (per-namespace isolation is the preferred multi-tenant model;\n64\t  confirm against the decision record's scoping outcome).\n65\t- Provide a configuration-level rollback path: the pgvector vector_io configuration must be\n66\t  revertible to the prior configuration without code changes if a regression is found, preserving a\n67\t  safety margin before inline providers are removed from the OGX distribution.\n68\t- Document that the default store is positioned for development experimentation; users with\n69\t  production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database.\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- Configuring a playground with RAG results in a namespace-scoped PostgreSQL/pgvector instance and\n74\t  an OGX instance using it via the remote pgvector vector_io provider, with no manual user setup\n75\t  steps.\n76\t- Deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources (Deployment, Service, PVC,\n77\t  Secret).\n78\t- Restarting the BFF neither orphans nor duplicates the provisioned instance; lifecycle behavior\n79\t  for pod restarts and credential rotation is implemented and tested.\n80\t- The provisioning code path is structured so a shared platform connection string can be consumed\n81\t  instead of self-provisioning without a rewrite (portability to the RHOAI 3.6 platform-provided\n82\t  database).\n83\t- OGX application storage remains on the SQLite default; only the vector_io provider configuration\n84\t  changes.\n85\t- The pgvector vector_io configuration can be reverted to the prior configuration without code\n86\t  changes (configuration-level rollback).\n87\t- Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows function against the provisioned instance with no loss of\n88\t  current capability, and all changes pass the odh-dashboard repository's existing build and CI\n89\t  pipeline.\n90\t\n91\t## HLR Traceability\n92\t\n93\t- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning)** — delivered by\n94\t  BFF self-provisioning.\n95\t- **AC-2 (Playground RAG workflows function, no loss of capability)** — provisioning and wiring are\n96\t  bundled here because they edit the same BFF code paths and configuration surface; splitting would\n97\t  double-touch the same call sites.\n98\t- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance)** — the PostgreSQL instance is an\n99\t  external process in the namespace, not an inline provider.\n100\t- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation)** — namespace-scoped provisioning.\n101\t- **AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments)** — sizing starts from the\n102\t  model-registry operator's PostgreSQL references, adjusted per the pgvector benchmark findings.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9636ee73fa8fca7","agent_id":"a3983a4f5ffc7ae27","session_id":"b07b26f1-905e-4b64-8357-872b48ad7853","uuid":"bfc05ee2-04f1-4a11-8c10-daaee6358f34","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:33:50.966Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a21ec3a40dc247f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
